      "response": {
        "category": "correctness",
        "consequence": "The `queued` value is wrong for every assignment source. It records the process start time, not when the assignment was queued. Any logic that uses it will misbehave.",
        "evidence_refs": [
          "source:new:src/sentry/integrations/services/assignment_source.py@sha256:885ab5f3b8ef5398cf84e90112d9352978908c663d9034ef89e7ed4eccfdfa0e"
        ],
        "explanation": "The field `queued: datetime = timezone.now()` calls `timezone.now()` once, when the class body runs at module import. Every AssignmentSource built through `from_integration` gets that same stale timestamp instead of its creation time. The field should use `field(default_factory=timezone.now)`. The datetime also reaches `asdict` in `to_dict` and is then passed as a Celery task kwarg (`assignment_source_dict`), where a raw datetime may fail JSON serialization. That second point is a risk I did not verify.",
        "lines": {
          "end_line": 18,
          "start_line": 18
        },
